<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HUMAN GOLD RUSH LESSON</p><h1>Technology & Research</h1><p class="intro">The proposed research system preserves study-relevant behavioral events while minimizing human input and avoiding heavy personal-data imports.</p><blockquote>How can technology preserve a reproducible dataset without building a surveillance system?</blockquote></header><aside class="notice"><strong>Important distinction</strong><p>Human-subjects classification, consent language, retention, withdrawal handling, and data release require review by the responsible IRB or authorized institutional officials.</p></aside><section class="content-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>Minimum human input</h2><p>Consent; participate, observe, or walk away; accept or reject; final destination yes or no; and exception actions such as dispute, correct, or withdraw.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>Automatic context</h2><p>The system supplies quarter, event, pseudonymous device, QR route, timestamp, approved location or proximity, role-at-event, state transition, consent version, schema version, and integrity hash.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>No heavy imports</h2><p>Exclude church rosters, merchant customer files, contact uploads, POS histories, social scraping, message-content analysis, banking records, voter files, and continuous location history.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>Research-ready preservation</h2><p>Maintain an append-only source log, protected identity-linkage vault, de-identified research dataset, public aggregate dataset, codebook, consent history, transformation record, and checksums.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h2>Proposal status</h2><p>AYSPS and Santa Fe Institute are prospective research audiences or collaborators. Publication must not imply institutional acceptance, sponsorship, IRB approval, or partnership until formally documented.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h2>Pre-genesis block</h2><p>The next few years are a pattern-testing period: every capture happens inside a 50-meter, 3-minute buyer/recipient and seller/sender handshake, confirmed through the <a href="proof-of-fulfillment.html">three distinct QR codes</a> — Identity, Trade, and Gratitude — before any wider rollout is considered.</p></div></article></section><section><div class="section-heading"><p>EVENT-DRIVEN RESEARCH</p><h2>One scan, one choice, one append-only event</h2></div><div class="flow"><div>Device registration</div><b>→</b><div>Consent</div><b>→</b><div>QR interaction</div><b>→</b><div>Human choice</div><b>→</b><div>Quarter dataset</div></div></section>